{
  "display_information": {
    "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
    "description": "An AI agent in a session its owner watches. While it listens, people on its roster tag it; it investigates, answers with evidence, acts.",
    "long_description": "TIER \u2014 STANDARD (the default, and the LEAST SECURE option here). ENABLES: everything \u2014 ingest, posting as the bot AND as you, real-time search, and answering in Slack when the bot is tagged. RISK: the highest of the reversible options \u2014 it grants write scopes on your OWN user token, so a message slopweaver sends is indistinguishable from one you typed. Take MINIMAL instead if that trade is not worth it to you. FIELDS TO POPULATE before pasting: {{APP_NAME}} and {{BOT_DISPLAY_NAME}} \u2014 set them to what you want this app and its bot called in Slack. FIRST INSTALL ONLY. A Slack manifest is applied whole: pasting this over an app that already exists renames it and its bot, and revokes every scope this file does not list. To change a live app, export its own manifest from api.slack.com/apps and edit that instead.",
    "name": "{{APP_NAME}}"
  },
